sha256:6d72f785c51e1485b643457d47b2600665fd98b553d84b305423c2c9cd4d41d4","download_count":637,"created_at":"2026-10-08T21:36:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T21:36:17Z"}],"body":"<!-- cliproxyapi-linux-release-assets:start -->\n## Linux release assets\n\n- `CLIProxyAPI_<version>_linux_<arch>.tar.gz` is the default Linux build. It supports dynamic library plugins and is built against a GLIBC 2.17 baseline.\n- `CLIProxyAPI_<version>_linux_<arch>_no-plugin.tar.gz` is the portable Linux build for musl-based or older systems such as OpenWrt. It does not support dynamic library plugins.\n\n## FreeBSD release assets\n\n- `CLIProxyAPI_<version>_freebsd_aarch64_no-plugin.tar.gz` is the FreeBSD arm64 build. It is built without CGO and does not support dynamic library plugins.\n\n<!-- cliproxyapi-linux-release-assets:end -->\n\n## Changelog\n\n- feat(openai): support response.interrupt in responses websocket handling (6331b38b)\n- fix(antigravity): include thoughts token count in openai completion tokens (ab151f5d)\n- fix(claude): ignore overage billing resets in unified rate limit parsing (80809679)\n- feat(claude): support responses compaction in claude executor (2bc236d2)\n- fix(claude): respect registry completion limit for default responses max tokens (a881c036)\n- fix(pluginhost): detach unselected plugins on config apply (67465884)\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/compare/v8.0.21...v8.0.22\n","reactions":{"total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0}}
